<title>HONDURAS: Honduras vows to proceed with disputed dam.</title>
<headline>Honduras vows to proceed with disputed dam.</headline>
<dateline>TEGUCIGALPA, Honduras 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honduran President Carlos Reina vowed on Thursday to go ahead with a project to construct a dam on the border with El Salvador despite claims it will flood farming land.</p>
<p>&quot;This region of the border has been the most forgotten of the country and we need to develop it,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
<p>El Salvador and Honduras signed a deal in 1993 to build the hydro-electric dam known as &quot;El Tigre&quot; (the Tiger) on the border.</p>
<p>But farmers, local authorities and environmentalists say the dam will flood extensive amounts of agricultural land.</p>
<p>The dam is expected to generate 700 megawatts of electricity.</p>
</text>
